-- title:
--   Local-unit criterion and valuation dichotomy over a place of ℚ̄
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and write $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbf Q$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $Pl$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ lying over $p$, in the sense that the image of $p$ lies in the nonunits of $Pl$, and let $\rho\colon\mathbf Z_{(p)}\to Pl$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with the inclusion $Pl\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbf Q}$ is the structure map of $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$; $Pl$ is regarded as a $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$-algebra via an instance whose structure map is assumed equal to $\rho$. Let $B$ be a commutative $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$-algebra of finite type and flat over $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$, put $T=Pl\otimes_{\mathbf Z_{(p)}}B$, and let $\mathfrak Q$ be a prime of $T$ whose contraction along $b\mapsto 1\otimes$-free inclusion $Pl\to T$ (`Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeft`) is the maximal ideal of $Pl$. Set $S=T_{\mathfrak Q}$, assumed to be a domain, let $toS\colon Pl\to S$ be the inclusion of $Pl$ into $T$ followed by the localisation map, and let $\mathfrak p=toS(\mathfrak m_{Pl})S$ be the ideal generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $Pl$, assumed prime. Let $K$ be a field that is a fraction field of $S$. Then: (i) every $h\in K$ which admits a representation $h\cdot c=a$ with $a,c\in S$ and $c\notin\mathfrak p$, and which for every prime $\mathfrak q$ of $S$ with $\mathfrak q\cap Pl=0$ (i.e. $\mathfrak q$ contracting to $\bot$ along $toS$) admits a representation $h\cdot s=a$ with $a,s\in S$, $s\notin\mathfrak q$, lies in the image of $S$ in $K$; and (ii) for every $h\in K$, at least one of $h$ and $h^{-1}$ admits a representation $h\cdot c=a$ (respectively $h^{-1}\cdot c=a$) with $a,c\in S$ and $c\notin\mathfrak p$, so that $S_{\mathfrak p}$ is a valuation ring of $K$.
--
--   This is the local-unit criterion together with the rank-one valuation dichotomy for the local ring of a flat finite-type $\mathbf Z_{(p)}$-algebra after base change to a (non-noetherian) valuation ring $Pl$ of $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ above $p$; the two halves are used respectively to recognise when a rational function on a model is regular at an integral point of the special fibre and to measure it along the branch determined by $\mathfrak p$. It is invoked in the analysis of the models `ModularCurve.XHDRLevel` and [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP`](def/ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP.html#L81), in particular when locating the primes of a crossing point and when evaluating products at the two branches.
